00:00:29.480 --> 00:00:34.770
a shortage for people who actually need this
medication for approved uses like lupus and

00:00:34.770 --> 00:00:40.600
malaria. It's unproven as a corona virus prophylactic.
And Trump doesn't have any of the conditions

00:00:40.600 --> 00:00:45.360
that this drug is actually approved to treat.
But he claims to be taking it. So last night,

00:00:45.360 --> 00:00:51.620
Nancy Pelosi, Democratic speaker of the House,
says, listen, this drug has adverse reactions

00:00:51.620 --> 00:00:56.930
under the sort of cardiac umbrella and Trump's
morbidly obese, so he shouldn't be taking

00:00:56.930 --> 00:01:01.579
it. Take a look at this.
As far as the president is concerned, the

00:01:01.579 --> 00:01:07.840
our our president and I would rather he not
be taking something that has not been approved

00:01:07.840 --> 00:01:15.290
by the scientists, especially in his age group
and in his, shall we say, weight group that

00:01:15.290 --> 00:01:22.140
is morbidly obese. So I I think that it's
not a good idea.

00:01:22.140 --> 00:01:29.280
So this immediately triggered a whole span
of reactions. Some people gleefully going

00:01:29.280 --> 00:01:35.060
all the way up to bordering on fat shaming
Trump. Other people reacted furious that Nancy

00:01:35.060 --> 00:01:40.470
Pelosi would be making such baseless claims
